# R-D9 (C# part), FIX-PLAN WP4 item 10: ak_bytes_free on a non-OK status
# date:        2026-09-24T16:13:46Z
# branch HEAD: 1c6996427bb0fc6f48165a6cf875dd6304f4ce90 (the slice changes are the commit that adds this log)
# core:        snapshot of ffi/poc/codec via 'git archive HEAD' (last core commit 6ede244),
#              built in scratch with --features "rpc count" into poc/csharp/target-core-count
#              libak_core.so sha256 cd329fa323eb2129...
# runtime:     .NET 8.0.31, SDK 8.0.131, Ubuntu 24.04 packages
# machine:     container, 4 vCPU, Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.10GHz
# code:        src/Rpc/CoreTransport.cs TakeOrThrow + CallBlocking; src/Rpc/Grid.cs try/finally; src/Rpc/Program.cs --error-path
# command:     dotnet src/Rpc/bin/Release/net8.0/akrpc.dll --error-path --calls 50
#
# The server serves /armonik.ffi.Bench/Down and not NoSuchMethod, so the second
# path returns UNIMPLEMENTED and the core reports a non-OK status on every
# delivery. The gate: every failed call throws, AND its forward crossing count
# equals the success path's (whole part; the queue drainer's idle 200 ms polls
# add a few crossings per row), because ak_bytes_free is one forward crossing
# and must be on both paths. Today's core returns an empty ak_bytes on failure,
# so the free releases nothing; the fix is that the binding no longer depends
# on that. No timing is taken or printed.

